<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Latif Mirza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1450</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd al-Latif Mirza was a Timurid prince, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulugh-beg">Ulugh Beg</a>. After quarrelling with his father over the succession, he defeated him in 1449 and had him put to death, then ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> for about six months before being assassinated in 1450 by his father's former retainers. His parricide earned him lasting infamy and deepened the fragmentation of Timurid power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>.</p></div>
